;--- this file configures each when to use ocr_enabled, assign a profile, and assign the components.
;--- component descriptions are in the ocr_profiles.ltx
;--- to break down what is assigned where...
; --- ocr_muzzle - flash hider, compensator, muzzle brake, or suppressor
; --- ocr_magazine - magazines
; --- ocr_barrel - barrels
; --- ocr_foregrip - VFG or AFG
; --- YOU CAN ONLY ASSIGN ONE PER SECTION ---

; --- suppressors have to be updated to a baseline to prevent the engines base multipliers from stacking when applied, this is setup toward the end.
; --- each suppressor needs a suppressor profile assigned to inheret the new multipliers, same way as any weapon used, example:
; --- ocr_muzzle = ocr_veteran_suppressor

;--- if you want to assign a new weapon, simply add it to the list like below, and attach the profile/components you want it to use. example:

;--- ![new_gun]
;--- ocr_enabled = true
;--- ocr_profile = ocr_m4
;--- ocr_muzzle = ocr_experienced_flashhider
;--- ocr_barrel = ocr_short_barrel
;--- ocr_foregrip = ocr_expert_vfg
;--- ocr_magazine = ocr_veteran_mag
;--- ocr_stock = ocr_normal_stock

;--- If any weapon is missing one of the sections, the script will treat it as a baseline 1.0, and no changes will be made.
;--- If a weapon has a built in suppressor, like the AS VAL, you can just assign ocr_veteran_suppressor, and it will simply use the suppressor as the base muzzle device.



